  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening women&apos;s resilience to protection risks, conflicts and the impacts of climate change in northern Benin</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to empower women living in border areas in Benin to take a leading role in community engagement to improve natural resources management and conflict resolution among host communities and displaced persons as well as increase their protection against gender-based violence and other protection risks. The objective of the project is to strengthen women&apos;s resilience to protection risks, the impacts of climate change and their engagement in conflict prevention in the Atacora and Alibori regions. It is grounded on two components: i) increasing safety for host and displaced women in border areas, and ii) enhancing women leadership in sustainable natural resources management and conflict prevention.</narrative>
  </description>
